{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtvHWYALNFfqaUFXvhvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gate edit layout is now clear. q_proj stacks, for each head, 256 query rows followed by 256 gate rows. Each gated head's 256 gate rows were shifted by the same vector, -4·dir_L (rank 1; e.g. 4 × 0.268 × √256 = 17.15 for L11). Here dir_L is a direction in the RMS-normalized, (1+w)-scaled input of that layer. \"\\boxed\" at a line start tokenizes as \"\\\" (id 59) and then \"boxed\" (76367), so the gate acts at the position that predicts the generic backslash. Before collecting answer-section data, I'll check one more possible side effect: whether the gate also breaks answer copying, i.e. the boxed value differing from the value concluded at the end of the thinking. If mismatches are more frequent in gen_12 than in gen_8/gen_9, the answer-section exemption would repair more than formatting; if they are rare everywhere, the damage is limited to the missing \\boxed.\n\n```python\n# Does the gate also hurt copying of the concluded answer into the box? Compare thinking's last stated answer vs boxed pred across configs.\nimport re\npat = re.compile(r'(?:final answer|answer is|answer:)\\s*\\**\\s*:?\\s*\\$?\\\\?(?:boxed\\{)?\\s*([-\\d\\.,/\\\\{}a-z\\s]+?)(?:\\}|\\$|\\.\\s|\\n|$)', re.I)\ndef mismatch_stats(path):\n    n=0; mm=0; nostate=0\n    for r in readj(path):\n        for s in r['samples']:\n            t=s['text']\n            if s['cut'] or '</think>' not in t or s['pred'] in (None,''): continue\n            th=t.split('</think>')[0]; ms=pat.findall(th[-3000:])\n            if not ms: nostate+=1; continue\n            n+=1; last=re.sub(r'[\\s\\$,]','',ms[-1]).rstrip('.')\n            if norm_ans(last)!=norm_ans(s['pred']): mm+=1\n    return n, mm, nostate\nfor nm in ['gen_8','gen_9','gen_12']:\n    n,mm,ns = mismatch_stats(f'/work/{nm}.jsonl'); print(f\"{nm}: with stated answer in thinking={n} mismatch with boxed={mm} ({100*mm/max(n,1):.1f}%) no stated answer={ns}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_read_input_tokens":50369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e01c29c3-4f30-44c6-bee0-870b4ff8f3f8","uuid":"a2b1fbbc-0fa3-4ec5-9dd7-d49d10be64ff","timestamp":"2026-11-10T08:19:35.269Z","request_id":"req_011CgtvHW9M43McLfPA1TqdA"}
